.TH tix-config-init 1  "init "
.SH NAME
tix\-config\-init \- Create the global config with prompts or explicit options
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtix config init\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-tickets\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-code\-directory\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-branch\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-github\-base\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-plugins\fR] [\fB\-\-default\-repository\-owner\fR] [\fB\-\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create the global config with prompts or explicit options
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to the global config file (overrides TIX_CONFIG_PATH and the platform default)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing config file
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the config that would be written, using the same inputs as initialization (with \-\-output json or toml, a plan carrying it)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output format for commands that support it (also forwarded to plugins as \-\-tix\-output)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
toml
.IP \(bu 2
default
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
\fB\-\-tickets\-directory\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Directory for tickets. Supply both directories to skip all prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-code\-directory\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Directory where repositories are cloned
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Set the log level to trace (shorthand for \-\-log\-level trace)
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\-prefix\fR \fI<BRANCH_PREFIX>\fR
Branch prefix for newly created worktrees
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Set the log level to warn (shorthand for \-\-log\-level warn)
.TP
\fB\-\-github\-base\-url\fR \fI<GITHUB_BASE_URL>\fR
Base URL for GitHub repositories
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-plugins\fR
Disable external plugin dispatch and plugin discovery in root help
.TP
\fB\-\-default\-repository\-owner\fR \fI<DEFAULT_REPOSITORY_OWNER>\fR
Owner to use for bare repository names
.TP
\fB\-\-repositories\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Repository aliases included in new tickets, comma\-separated or repeated
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
